--- a/docs/control-protocol.md
+++ b/docs/control-protocol.md
@@ -1,5 +1,31 @@
 # Control protocol
 
+## Plervo authentication and limits
+
+The control channel is off by default and binds only `127.0.0.1`. In Plervo builds,
+`--control PORT` also requires `--control-token-file FILE` (or
+`PLERVO_SLIDES_CONTROL_TOKEN_FILE`). Create a new 256-bit random token for each session,
+keep the file private, and never place the token itself in a command argument or log.
+For example, on macOS/Linux:
+
+```sh
+umask 077
+openssl rand -hex 32 > /private/session/slides.token
+plervo-slides --control 7990 --control-token-file /private/session/slides.token
+plervo-slides-cli mcp --connect 7990 --control-token-file /private/session/slides.token
+```
+
+Create the private session directory first. On Windows, keep the token in a directory
+accessible only to your account. Unix token files with group/other access and symlinked
+files are rejected. Every JSON request must include a `token` field; the official CLI
+adds it from the file. Unauthenticated requests never reach the UI.
+
+There are at most four client connections, 1 MiB per request, 1,024 requests per
+connection, and a 10-second socket idle timeout. A connection can be reopened by the
+client. Lost responses do not automatically replay commands, because an edit may have
+already succeeded; inspect the document before retrying.
+
+
 Start the app with `--control <port>`. The server listens on `127.0.0.1` only and speaks JSON
 lines: one request object per line, one reply per line.
 
